        "Id" : "Gear_Cockpit_Sensor_Array_4",
        "Name" : "Sensor Array +4",
        "Details" : "Sensor Arrays increase the range at which targets can be visually acquired for direct targeting and spotting for support fire.  Sensor modules are clusters of sensor arrays that work in sync with each other and are integrated into one component that is more compact and efficient.  Multiple sensor modules and arrays have a cumulative effect.  While being made with high-tech lightweight electronics that overall don't add any substantial tonnage to a battlemech, sensor arrays and modules slightly stress the battlemech's engine and coolant systems, drawing power and coolant from such to the point that the battlemech's threshold for shutting down from overheating is slightly reduced.  This is a small price to pay for what this upgrade does, but this price tag can accumulate a bit when many upgrades are installed in a battlemech.  Coolant plants and other upgrades that raise the shutdown threshold will counter the accumulated stress on a battlemech's coolant systems from these upgrades.\n\nSPECIAL GAME NOTE:  Having a total increase that is too high will make the game lag and stutter during battles.",
